{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5495: implement additional features for `cmd/b2sum` in the go-unix-utils project. The task is a \"stitch\" code generation task targeting srd076 requirements R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, and R3.1. The specific requirements from the task description are:\n   - R1: Implement srd076 R2.1 — check mode that reads checksums from a file, parses each line (GNU or BSD tag format), recomputes BLAKE2b digest, and compares\n   - R2: Implement srd076 R2.2 — print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry, exit 1 if any check fails\n   - R3: Implement srd076 R2.3 — --warn prints warning for malformed lines, --quiet suppresses OK lines, --status suppresses all output\n   - R4: Implement srd076 R3.1 — -b marks binary mode (\"HASH *FILENAME\"), -t (default) uses text mode (\"HASH  FILENAME\")\n   \n   Design decisions require using `pkg/hashutil.FormatBSDTag` for tagged output, adjusting `HashConfig.DigestLen` when digest length flag is specified, and using `pkg/hashutil.VerifyChecksums` for check mode.\n\n   The file note says: \"Add BSD tag format, variable digest length, and check mode verification.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - BLAKE2b hashing with variable digest length (golang.org/x/crypto/blake2b)\n   - GNU checksum format vs BSD tag format\n   - pkg/hashutil shared library for hash computation, formatting, and verification\n   - Differential testing against GNU reference binary (gb2sum)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Flag parsing without cobra (manual arg parsing)\n   - HashConfig struct with Algorithm, NewHash function, and DigestLen fields\n   - CheckOptions struct with Warn, Quiet, Status fields\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd076-b2sum.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for b2sum with requirements R1 (digest computation), R2 (check mode), R3 (output format/digest length), R4 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - Key requirement R3.3: \"--length=N sets digest length in bits. N must be positive multiple of 8 and at most 512. Default 512. Exit 1 if invalid.\"\n     - Key requirement R1.3: \"--tag must use BSD-style 'BLAKE2b (FILENAME) = HASH'. When --length specified, tag name includes bit length e.g. 'BLAKE2b-256'\"\n     - Non-goals: No BLAKE2s, no keyed hashing/MAC mode\n\n   - `cmd/b2sum/main.go` (READ - existing 125-line implementation to be MODIFIED)\n     - Already has: SIGPIPE handler, basic arg parsing, check mode via hashutil.VerifyChecksums, digest mode via hashutil.DigestFiles\n     - Already parses: --binary/-b, --text/-t, --tag, --check/-c, --warn/-w, --quiet, --status\n     - MISSING: --length flag parsing entirely, DigestLen hardcoded to 64, Algorithm hardcoded to \"BLAKE2b\", newBLAKE2b always creates 512-bit hash\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"hash\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"golang.org/x/crypto/blake2b\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     func newBLAKE2b() hash.Hash {\n         h, _ := blake2b.New512(nil)\n         return h\n     }\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         cfg := hashutil.HashConfig{\n             Algorithm: \"BLAKE2b\",\n             NewHash:   newBLAKE2b,\n             DigestLen: 64,\n         }\n         if opts.check {\n             checkOpts := hashutil.CheckOptions{Warn: opts.warn, Quiet: opts.quiet, Status: opts.status}\n             exitCode := 0\n             for _, f := range files {\n                 ok, err := hashutil.VerifyChecksums(f, cfg, checkOpts, os.Stdout, os.Stderr)\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"b2sum: %s\\n\", err)\n                     exitCode = 1\n                 } else if !ok {\n                     exitCode = 1\n                 }\n             }\n             os.Exit(exitCode)\n         }\n         os.Exit(hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, os.Stdout, os.Stderr))\n     }\n     type options struct {\n         binary bool; tag bool; check bool; warn bool; quiet bool; status bool\n     }\n     func parseArgs(args []string) (options, []string) { /* manual flag parsing */ }\n     func parseLongFlag(arg string, opts *options) (bool, int) { /* --binary, --text, --tag, --check, --warn, --quiet, --status */ }\n     func parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) int { /* -b, -t, -c, -w */ }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/hashutil/` (from package_contracts - NOT read from filesystem)\n     - Key exports: HashConfig{Algorithm, NewHash, DigestLen}, FormatBSDTag(algorithm, filename, digest), VerifyChecksums(checksumFile, cfg, opts, stdout, stderr), DigestFiles(files, cfg, binary, tag, stdout, stderr), CheckOptions{Warn, Quiet, Status}\n     - FormatBSDTag signature: `func FormatBSDTag(algorithm, filename, digest string) string`\n     - DigestFiles signature: `func DigestFiles(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int`\n\n   - `cmd/sha256sum/main.go` (listed as required reading but NOT yet read)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Work was in the reading/planning phase.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   The main implementation gap identified is the `--length` flag. The existing code already handles most features (check mode, binary/text mode, tag mode, warn/quiet/status). The key additions needed are:\n   - Parse `--length=N` and `--length N` flag forms\n   - Validate N: positive, multiple of 8, ≤ 512\n   - Create blake2b hash with variable output size (use `blake2b.New(N/8, nil)` instead of `blake2b.New512(nil)`)\n   - Set `cfg.DigestLen = N/8`\n   - Set `cfg.Algorithm = \"BLAKE2b-N\"` when N != 512 (for tag format per R1.3)\n   - Add `length int` field to options struct\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive task description message containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specs, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. The task is to implement srd076 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R3.1 for cmd/b2sum.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify `cmd/b2sum/main.go` to add:\n     - `--length=N` flag parsing (both `--length=N` and `--length N` forms)\n     - Length validation (positive, multiple of 8, ≤ 512, exit 1 on invalid)\n     - Variable BLAKE2b constructor based on length\n     - Algorithm name adjustment for tag format (\"BLAKE2b-256\" etc.)\n     - Add `length` field to options struct\n   - Verify: `go build -o bin/b2sum ./cmd/b2sum/` succeeds\n   - Verify: `go vet ./cmd/b2sum/` passes\n   - Run tests to confirm acceptance criteria\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two key files (srd076-b2sum.yaml and cmd/b2sum/main.go) and was about to begin implementation. I had identified what exists vs what needs to be added. The existing code already handles check mode, binary/text mode, tag mode, and warn/quiet/status flags. The primary missing feature is the `--length` flag for variable digest length, along with associated validation and hash constructor changes. Most of the task requirements (R1-R4 in the task, mapping to srd076 R2.1-R2.3, R3.1) appear to already be implemented in the existing code except for `--length` support.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the modified `cmd/b2sum/main.go` with the `--length` flag support added. This involves:\n   1. Adding `length int` field to the `options` struct\n   2. Adding `--length=N` / `--length N` parsing to `parseLongFlag`\n   3. Adding length validation in `main()` (positive, multiple of 8, ≤ 512)\n   4. Creating a variable-length BLAKE2b constructor function\n   5. Adjusting `cfg.Algorithm` to include bit length when not 512\n   6. Adjusting `cfg.DigestLen` to `length/8`\n   7. Then running `go build -o bin/b2sum ./cmd/b2sum/` and `go vet ./cmd/b2sum/` to verify\n\n   The task description states: \"Add BSD tag format, variable digest length, and check mode verification\" as the file modification note, and the acceptance criteria require: AC1 (build succeeds), AC2 (vet passes), AC3 (tag output produces BSD-style), AC4 (variable digest length works), AC5 (check mode reports verification results).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5495/7f1b0926-f3d6-48cd-808e-21c806523a9b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f1b0926-f3d6-48cd-808e-21c806523a9b","uuid":"a2756ce7-5451-4e68-ad6f-33773a98f75f","timestamp":"2026-05-23T01:27:36.158Z","isSynthetic":true}
