{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WUTSAQUmjGkt6LZ4HxsxmU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All clean. Here's what was implemented in `cmd/b2sum/main.go`:\n\n1. **`--length=N` / `--length N` flag parsing** — new `parseLengthFlag` function handles both forms, with error messages on invalid or missing values\n2. **Length validation** — rejects values that are ≤0, not a multiple of 8, or >512, exiting with code 1\n3. **Variable-length BLAKE2b constructor** — `newBLAKE2b(size)` returns a closure that creates a BLAKE2b hash with the specified byte size via `blake2b.New`\n4. **Algorithm name adjustment** — uses `\"BLAKE2b-N\"` (e.g., `\"BLAKE2b-256\"`) in tag format when length differs from the default 512\n5. **Dynamic `DigestLen`** — sets `cfg.DigestLen` to `length/8`\n\nThe existing check mode (R2.1, R2.2, R2.3) and binary/text mode (R3.1) support was already correctly wired up via `hashutil.VerifyChecksums` and `hashutil.DigestFiles`. All outputs match the GNU reference binary `gb2sum` byte-for-byte."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":143,"cache_read_input_tokens":36639,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":143},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f1b0926-f3d6-48cd-808e-21c806523a9b","uuid":"e1635f00-cf69-47df-8183-223dfa7f0925"}
